Hi,

Is there an 'INLA way' of specifying a transformation of the response
variable in order to meet the requirements of a specific likelihood? So
that when new response values are predicted, a backtransformation is
applied as well.

An example is modelling a strictly negative response using a gamma
likelihood, where a reversal of the sign would be sufficient. The case
at hand is groundwater depth below soil surface, which is typically
expressed as negative numbers.

Thanks

Floris

