Dear r-inla people,

I was trying to use the New England example
on the new r-inla.org <http://r-inla.org> website

https://sites.google.com/a/r-inla.org/www/examples/case-studies/martino-akerkar-and-rue-2010/leukemia-example

(with the “Besag” model)

Now the links “dataset”  and “graph.file” seem corrupted on this page.

In any case I found the “Leuk” dataset
within the INLA package,  which also
contains the spatial polygon object nwEngland.
So after some searching on your FAQ page, I gather that

poly2nb(nwEngland)

should give me the adjacency matrix.  But this function throws an error:

Error in sum(sapply(foundInBox, length)) :

  Invalid
‘type’ (list) of argument.

I did some further searching and as far as
I can see the poly2nb function should be able to deal with spatial
polygons.  I couldn’t find in the
inla.pdf info how to do it either.

Any suggestion what I am overlooking?

Best,

Bart

